September 16, 2026, v1.18
- fixed: no product name, product version and build version was printed for a
  mounted Mac OS X Install CD/DVD image, because the name of the plist file was
  passed to print_xml_info instead of the content of the plist file; a
  regression that was introduced with v1.10 when print_xml_info was changed
  from reading a file to taking the xml content
- fixed: an install stub printed a "No such file or directory" error on stderr,
  because the SystemVersion.plist was read even if nothing had been mounted
- fixed: "Install Mac OS X Lion.app" was never found without program
  arguments, because a Spotlight pattern is anchored at the beginning of the
  file name and therefore "Install OS X *.app" cannot match it
- fixed: the exit code was always 0, even if nothing could be read at all; the
  script exits with 1 now if at least one installer could not be investigated
- fixed: a failed "hdiutil attach" went unnoticed, the script printed the path
  followed by an empty line and no error message at all
- fixed: an installer path that contains *, ? or [ ] could be garbled, because
  the pathname expansion was still active
- fixed: a path without the .app suffix was cut at the last dot, so that a dot
  in one of the parent folders led to a wrong app name
- fixed: a path that does not exist was reported as an unsupported macOS
  release instead of a missing folder
- fixed: the "Resource busy" check was missing for the
  "/Volumes/Shared Support" mount point that the Big Sur and Monterey
  installers leave open
- fixed: pressing Ctrl-C left the BaseSystem and InstallESD mount points behind
- fixed: the MobileAsset archive was passed to unzip without checking that it
  exists and that there is exactly one of them
- changed: informational and error messages go to stderr now, stdout contains
  the header line and the version info only

